(1632971, 221015, 11467, '<td valign="top">I think there are a couple of small problems with this image.<br/>Firstly the lighting seems to be a combination of 2 or more different lighting types. The background is daylight or flourescent, and the foreground is possible tungsteon.  This makes a yellow glow. On my monitor the face looks a little green.<br/>Black &amp; white can overcome this problem.<br/>Also the face seems a little plasticy, the skin seems unnaturally smooth (Take that as a compliment if you didn''t do it in an editing program).  I think B&amp;W would help here also as  part of the problem is the colour of the face. <br/>The black background is great and arm positions are good for a natural pose.</td>', 'I think there are a couple of small problems with this image.Firstly the lighting seems to be a combination of 2 or more different lighting types. The background is daylight or flourescent, and the foreground is possible tungsteon.  This makes a yellow glow. On my monitor the face looks a little green.Black & white can overcome this problem.Also the face seems a little plasticy, the skin seems unnaturally smooth (Take that as a compliment if you didn''t do it in an editing program).  I think B&W would help here also as  part of the problem is the colour of the face. The black background is great and arm positions are good for a natural pose.', '2005-08-22 19:32:03.000000', NULL, 1),
