lly submitted for this challenge... <br/><a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=224208" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/4564/thumb/224208.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/4564/thumb/224208.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/4564/thumb/224208.jpg"/></a> <br/>But then I realized how much similar it was to <a href="//dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=200" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">grigrigirl</a>''s winner shot of Nude II<br/> <a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=99123" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/248/thumb/99123.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/248/thumb/99123.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/248/thumb/99123.jpg"/></a> <br/> and I decided to remove my entry. When I shot it, the similarity with grigrigirl''s shot was not intentional.  But grigrigirl was the first to introduce it on DPC and won a ribbon with it, so out of respect for her  and because I didn''t want people to think I copied her, I deliberatly chose another entry to submit for NUDE III.  And while I was at it, I decided to go "the DrJones way" , if you know what I mean. LOL!  <br/> <br/>Again, congrats to the winners. Fierce competition! ;-)  And see you at NUDE IV! ;-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-29 13:10:40.</i></td>', 'Thanks everyone for the great comments and Bravo to the winners. Here are some of my outtakes:      And the following outtake is the one I originally submitted for this challenge...  But then I realized how much similar it was to grigrigirl''s winner shot of Nude II   and I decided to remove my entry. When I shot it, the similarity with grigrigirl''s shot was not intentional.  But grigrigirl was the first to introduce it on DPC and won a ribbon with it, so out of 