(1658928, 220146, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by musze:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 1olddawg:</b></div><hr/><i> When I first viewed this image I gave it a seven. And looking at it again now I still say seven. Just wondering how many would vote ten if this was a 300 pound guy with the exact same lighting and poise??? </i></td></tr></table>lol, u make a good point. it is very sad. i however don''t look at photography that way. an art teacher (drawing I in college) of mine told me that she even prefered to draw large people because they have much more to work with...oh well....just my .02. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Maybe if you want to push your creative buttons as an exercise perhaps but that''ll just be a tune up for when you shoot a more attractive model because that''s what will get the accolades as this contest further illustrates.</td>', 'Originally posted by musze: Originally posted by 1olddawg: When I first viewed this image I gave it a seven. And looking at it again now I still say seven. Just wondering how many would vote ten if this was a 300 pound guy with the exact same lighting and poise??? lol, u make a good point. it is very sad. i however don''t look at photography that way. an art teacher (drawing I in college) of mine told me that she even prefered to draw large people because they have much more to work with...oh well....just my .02.   Maybe if you want to push your creative buttons as an exercise perhaps but that''ll just be a tune up for when you shoot a more attractive model because that''s what will get the accolades as this contest further illustrates.', '2005-08-30 19:07:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659144, 220108, 31606, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done.  I even like the original you posted.  I like everything about this shot.  Congrats on 11th place.  Should have been top 3 IMO.</td>', 'Very nicely done.  I even like the original you posted.  I like everything about this shot.  Congrats on 11th place.  Should have been top 3 IMO.', '2005-08-30 20:40:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659167, 218759, 649, '<td valign="top">The best I have seen you do.</td>', 'The best I have seen you do.', '2005-08-30 20:47:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659420, 220844, 34659, '<td valign="top">Is this you?  Whether it is or not, I must reiterate what I said before...  This is a GREAT shot.  VERY underrated in my personal opinion (I scored it an 8).  I love the fact that the blindfold is the "color" of sin - red and that it hides the model''s face from the perceived "sin" of the shot.  I just thought this spoke on so many levels, it was extremely well thought-out and presented.  I have to agree that the lighting is really the only short-coming of the shot.  I wasn''t exactly sure what it was keeping me from scoring it a 10, but that''s it.  Maybe a tad bit more contrast and dodge/burn brush (although I''m not trying to sound like a preacher for Heida and/or Joey - although I truly admire their talents!).  This was a seriously great shot - took a lot of courage and fortitude to stick by, but in my humble opinion any qualms about it were shallow minds and the far too accepted anorexic viewpoint of beauty.  In all honesty, it reminded me of a modern-day Renoir.</td>', 'Is this you?  Whether it is or not, I must reiterate what I said before...  This is a GREAT shot.  VERY underrated in my personal opinion (I scored it an 8).  I love the fact that the blindfold is the "color" of sin - red and that it hides the model''s face from the perceived "sin" of the shot.  I just thought this spoke on so many levels, it was extremely well thought-out and presented.  I have to agree that the lighting is really the only short-coming of the shot.  I wasn''t exactly sure what it was keeping me from scoring it a 10, but that''s it.  Maybe a tad bit more contrast and dodge/burn brush (although I''m not trying to sound like a preacher for Heida and/or Joey - although I truly admire their talents!).  This was a seriously great shot - took a lot of courage and fortitude to stick by, but in my humble opinion any qualms about it were shallow minds and the far too accepted anorexic viewpoint of beauty.  In all honesty, it reminded me of a modern-day Renoir.', '2005-08-30 21:49:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659473, 221055, 36068, '<td valign="top">Ok so I have to say....if this is you, this took some guts!!</td>', 'Ok so I have to say....if this is you, this took some guts!!', '2005-08-30 22:07:37.000000', NULL, 0),
