(1659547, 220146, 6900, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 1olddawg:</b></div><hr/><i> When I first viewed this image I gave it a seven. And looking at it again now I still say seven. Just wondering how many would vote ten if this was a 300 pound guy with the exact same lighting and poise??? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>lol<br/> <br/>Kidding, right?  I just wonder how many people would have given Heida''s Angel a 10 if it was me with my arms on the rocks standing there.  Good looking models add to the beauty of a picture.  If it was a 300 pound model it would have gotten humor points for me, but the PULL of the photo would have been different.  I tend to vote on emotion and impact the photo makes on me - this one pulls me.  A 300 pound guy in the same pose would not do the same.</td>', 'Originally posted by 1olddawg: When I first viewed this image I gave it a seven. And looking at it again now I still say seven. Just wondering how many would vote ten if this was a 300 pound guy with the exact same lighting and poise???   lol Kidding, right?  I just wonder how many people would have given Heida''s Angel a 10 if it was me with my arms on the rocks standing there.  Good looking models add to the beauty of a picture.  If it was a 300 pound model it would have gotten humor points for me, but the PULL of the photo would have been different.  I tend to vote on emotion and impact the photo makes on me - this one pulls me.  A 300 pound guy in the same pose would not do the same.', '2005-08-30 22:34:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659550, 221052, 10634, '<td valign="top">Don''t give up.... I think the lighting and positioning were what hurt this. Keep trying.... BTW I like hairy butts too  ;-)</td>', 'Don''t give up.... I think the lighting and positioning were what hurt this. Keep trying.... BTW I like hairy butts too  ;-)', '2005-08-30 22:35:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659569, 220472, 10634, '<td valign="top">This is such a nice image. It was a wonderful attempt. It would be interesting to see if your wife would be willing to reshoot so you could see the difference had the focus been on her face. Keep everything else the same, but get her face and eyes.</td>', 'This is such a nice image. It was a wonderful attempt. It would be interesting to see if your wife would be willing to reshoot so you could see the difference had the focus been on her face. Keep everything else the same, but get her face and eyes.', '2005-08-30 22:40:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659580, 220001, 10634, '<td valign="top">Sorry I didn''t have time to comment during the challenge. This was an excellent idea and I just loved it. I think the softening filter may be what hurt you. Perhaps if the contrast, etc had been upped a bit, but the way it is, it looks like the softness was a mistake or from compression.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-30 21:47:09.</i></td>', 'Sorry I didn''t have time to comment during the challenge. This was an excellent idea and I just loved it. I think the softening filter may be what hurt you. Perhaps if the contrast, etc had been upped a bit, but the way it is, it looks like the softness was a mistake or from compression.', '2005-08-30 22:46:52.000000', '2005-08-30 22:47:09.000000', 0),
(1659596, 221090, 10634, '<td valign="top">After breastfeeding four kids, those could be mine. :-) Sorry I didn''t get to comment on this during the challenge, but here it goes. I think the biggest distraction here is the fabric bunched beneath her breasts. It makes it look as though she were at Mardi Gras and just decided to flash the camera. The pose is rather bland as well. When I see this shot, I think of the Calendar Girls in England. A different pose, with an appropriate prop and B&amp;W would work. This woman makes me think "classic." I don''t know why.</td>', 'After breastfeeding four kids, those could be mine. :-) Sorry I didn''t get to comment on this during the challenge, but here it goes. I think the biggest distraction here is the fabric bunched beneath her breasts. It makes it look as though she were at Mardi Gras and just decided to flash the camera. The pose is rather bland as well. When I see this shot, I think of the Calendar Girls in England. A different pose, with an appropriate prop and B&W would work. This woman makes me think "classic." I don''t know why.', '2005-08-30 22:53:57.000000', NULL, 0),
